{
  "description": "A family-aware diagnostic adapter for Self-EvolveRec that measures the trained NextItNet model through the host ModelView interface and produces an interpretation prompt grounded in measured metrics and explicit definitions.",
  "motivation": "Guide model improvements using reproducible evidence while preserving NextItNet compatibility, fixed benchmark conditions, and the single-model-per-category requirement.",
  "implementation_notes": "Retain DiagnosisProbe(view, device), run_full_diagnosis(train_loader), and diagnosis_interpreter_prompt(raw_diagnosis). Consume batches shaped B × L containing sequence, positive, and negative tensors. Access the actual network through view.model and preserve item_emb, log2feats, and predict_score compatibility. Mask padding and invalid targets; use the final nonpadding position for left-padded histories, never count−1. Use only available histories, titles, descriptions, and timestamps. Mark unavailable review information and simulator traits as unobserved. Generate full-catalog unseen-item recommendations for five training users per category. Select models using macro validation HR@10 across all four categories; diagnostic proxies must not replace that metric. Keep inference and the embedded predictor writer consistent with each category’s single trained checkpoint.",
  "pseudocode": "class DiagnosisProbe(view, device):\n    run_full_diagnosis(train_loader):\n        preserve model training state\n        set view.model to evaluation mode\n        under no_grad:\n            for _, sequence, positive, negative in train_loader:\n                features = view.log2feats(sequence)\n                identify valid positions and targets\n                measure defined diagnostics using features and view.predict_score\n            aggregate measurements with explicit denominators\n        restore model training state\n        return {metrics, metric_definitions}\n\ndef diagnosis_interpreter_prompt(raw_diagnosis):\n    include measured metrics and their definitions\n    distinguish observations from hypotheses\n    state unavailable information explicitly\n    request NextItNet-compatible, single-model improvement hypotheses",
  "originality": {
    "score": 3,
    "positive": "Combines a stable diagnostic interface with family-specific probes and evidence-grounded interpretation.",
    "negative": "The description specifies an integration contract rather than a new diagnostic algorithm or demonstrated scientific contribution."
  },
  "future_potential": {
    "score": 7,
    "positive": "Could support repeatable diagnosis and targeted architecture or optimization experiments across sequential recommendation models.",
    "negative": "Its usefulness depends on choosing reliable diagnostic measurements and validating proposed improvements; no effectiveness results are supplied."
  },
  "code_difficulty": {
    "score": 5,
    "positive": "The required interfaces and batch structure make the adapter straightforward to organize.",
    "negative": "Correct padding masks, score shapes, aggregation, model-state restoration, and predictor consistency require careful implementation."
  }
}
